{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nTen ADRs carry operator procedure alongside their decision. `infra/runbooks/` already holds 21 runbooks (`git ls-tree origin/main -- infra/runbooks`). Most procedures already exist there in fuller form; the ADR copies are the drift.\n\n## Approach\n| ADR | Procedural lines (origin/main) | Target | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0012 | `:34-36` bootstrap teardown caution; `:105-108` two-step apply + seven secrets | existing `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md` §\"Provision from scratch\" (`:88-113`) | add the teardown caution to step 1; replace ADR `:105-108` with `See infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §\"Provision from scratch\".` |\n| 0048 | `:30-33` import mechanics, `:51-54` state-rm + `RE-HOMED-TO-REBAR.md` marker, `:68-70` operator follow-ups | existing `infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md`, new section `## Re-homing mechanics (from ADR 0048)` placed before `## Secrets` (`:67`) | move; ADR keeps decision clauses 1–6 as one sentence each + pointer |\n| 0079 | `:61-65` Back-out incl. \"units ship DISABLED; enable after a manual dry-run\" | existing `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"Continuous auto-deploy (epic 88ab / story 8903)\" (`:522`), whose `**Back-out (disable auto-deploy):**` paragraph is at `:563` | add the ship-disabled/dry-run sentence there; ADR `## Back-out` body → pointer. Amendments (`:74-128`) stay (rationale). |\n| 0085 | `:58-71` eventual-consistency discipline, `:73-79` report procedure | NEW `infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md` (how to run `scripts/run_live_matrix.py`, `pytest -m live`, env vars, report paths, index-lag rules, leak log) | move; ADR keeps §1–§2 + pointer. Also fix `scripts/run_live_matrix.py:2` docstring \"ADR 0037 §4\" → \"ADR 0085 (archived into ADR 0121 §20); runbook infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md\". |\n| 0031 | `:158-165` Operator break-glass (clear a wedged `refs/reconciler/lock`) | existing `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"The reconciler cursor\" (`:252`) | move the two commands; ADR keeps pointer (the only procedure inside the consolidation set). CORRECTED: this row previously cited `:158-168`, 3 lines past the section's end, which swallows the `## Lease self-healing (C2 — extends this module)` heading at `:167` — deleting that range would have silently decapitated the next section. The section is `:158-165`; `:166` is blank. |\n| 0105 | `:94-97` \"A one-time operator cutover is required… Until that runs…\" | existing `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` §REMEDIATE (`:140-185`) already holds the procedure | replace the bullet with `The one-time cutover ran — task gnarly-sinistrous-groundhog (097b-de23-bf12-4c38); procedure and scrub: infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md §REMEDIATE.` |\n| 0109 | `:112-123` tier-selection table (already single-sourced at `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Validating a gate change: which replay tier\"), `:125-139` cost table | NEW `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md` §\"Replay tiers: invocation and budget\" (`python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0|tier1|tier2 …`, cost table, cap/ledger) | move cost table; replace §6 table with pointer to the gate doc; keep §6's \"required, not advisory\" sentence and the `plan-review-eval:` trailer convention |\n| 0113 | `:85-93` change-triggered execution (`eval-changed-rubrics` job, `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml:54`), `:95-109` heal-loop schedule + `unreliable-criterion:` ticket handling | same NEW `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md` §\"Heal loop and the unreliable-criterion breaker\" (`rebar criteria heal [--dry-run]`, ledger `.rebar/fixture_heal_ledger.jsonl`, how a human resolves a breaker ticket) | move the operating steps; ADR keeps decisions 6–7 as rules + pointer |\n| 0112 | `:241-252` Open items (all resolved: S1–S6 children of epic `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897` closed; cap procedures at `review-bot-ops.md:876,1008,1127,1240` — the four `## … (ADR 0112 / story …)` sections — and `gate-scratch-mount.md`) | existing runbooks (no new text) | replace `## Open items` with `## Open items — resolved` naming the closing story per item and the runbook sections; keep Decisions 1–7 verbatim (cited by number from `infra/scripts/*.sh`, `docs/config.md:657,676`) |\n| 0059 | `:613-633` §8 Bedrock model-id trap set; `:666-693` §10 compose line anchors and the \"read d2ce before quoting\" status | existing `infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md` §\"Which model id to use\" (`:133`) gets the trap list; `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` §\"Kill-switch: revert the LLM path from Bedrock to direct Anthropic\" (`:374`) gets the current-wiring paragraph | move; ADR keeps one-sentence findings + pointers. Write \"the removed `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`\" in the runbook (`tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py:115-150` scans `review-bot-ops.md` for removal context). §9 and \"Evidence-hygiene rules\" stay (findings, not procedure). |\n\nCurrent vocabulary only (`bridge status`, never `bridge-status`) in both newly written runbook text **and every line this story MOVES into a runbook**: the stale-vocabulary scan's `_HISTORY_PREFIXES` exempts `docs/adr/`, but NOT `infra/runbooks/`, so prose that was unscanned inside an ADR becomes scanned the moment it lands in a runbook. Any legacy spelling carried along by a move must be updated as part of the move. Cite modules/CLI, never `docs/experiments/...` paths (eval-harness epic moves them).\n\n## Scope\nEdit ADRs: `docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md`, `0031-reconciler-ref-lock.md`, `0048-rehome-snap-shared-infra.md`, `0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md`, `0079-autodeploy-on-box-timer.md`, `0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md`, `0105-ssm-secrets-never-in-terraform-state.md`, `0109-plan-review-replay-harness.md`, `0112-on-box-disk-ceiling-architecture.md`, `0113-fixture-mining-and-admission-protocol.md`. Edit runbooks: `infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md`, `sso-auth-host.md`, `review-bot-ops.md`, `ssm-secret-write-only.md`, `bedrock-access.md`. New: `infra/runbooks/reconciler-live-matrix.md`, `infra/runbooks/plan-review-eval-ops.md`. Also `scripts/run_live_matrix.py` (docstring).\n\n## Testing\n`python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` (runbook links resolve); `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`; `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check`; `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`; `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py::test_no_prose_doc_advertises_the_variable_as_live tests/unit/test_plan_review_docs.py tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py`; `pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/ -k bridge_vocabulary_stale` (a SEPARATE invocation: `-k` filters the whole run, so folding it in with the modules above would silently deselect them; the selector is used instead of the module path because story `b721-6c6d-504e-45da` renames `test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py` in place to `test_bridge_vocabulary_stale.py`, and the two stories sit in different epics with no ordering link — the selector collects the same 9 tests under either name); `ruff check scripts/run_live_matrix.py`.\n\n**Line numbers for ADRs 0031 and 0085 are measured BEFORE story S3 (`8257-3a28`) runs, and S3 shifts them.** They are the table's only rows inside S3's 20-ADR set; S3 rewrites each original's status line and inserts an archive banner above the body, shifting every line below it. This story runs after S3, so those citations will NOT hold against the tree it edits. Anchor on content: locate the `### Operator break-glass` heading in 0031, and the `### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes` and `### 4. Report` headings in 0085, taking each section through to the line before the next `#`-prefixed heading. Re-measure and restate those 3 ranges as the first implementation step. The other 7 ADRs in the table (0012, 0048, 0059, 0079, 0105, 0109, 0113) are outside S3's set, so their line numbers are unaffected. The 0085 ranges `:58-71` and `:73-79` were re-measured today and are correct as written against the pre-S3 tree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] For each of the ten listed ADRs, `grep -c 'infra/runbooks/' docs/adr/<file>` ≥ 1 and the moved line ranges above no longer appear (`git diff -U0` shows them removed).\n- [ ] The two new runbooks exist and every `](…)` in them resolves (`check_docs_index.py --check` exit 0).\n- [ ] `grep -n 'ADR 0037' scripts/run_live_matrix.py` is empty; `grep -n 'Open items$' docs/adr/0112-*.md` is empty."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793518245031366001,"uuid":"7327aa5c-17e5-4e2b-b59b-b787de377e1a"}